  Slug: scoundrel
  DisplayName: Scoundrel
  IconPath: systems/pf2e/icons/features/classes/scoundrel.webp
  Description: You use fast-talking, flattery, and a silver tongue to avoid danger
    and escape tricky situations. You might be a grifter or con artist, or you might
    use your skills in certain reputable professions, like a barrister or diplomat.
    When you successfully @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Feint], the target
    is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Off-Guard] against your melee attacks
    until the end of your next turn. On a critical success, the target is off-guard
    against all melee attacks until the end of your next turn, not just yours. If
    you Feint while wielding an agile or finesse melee weapon, you can step immediately
    after the Feint as a free action. You're trained in Deception and Diplomacy.
    You can choose Charisma as your key attribute.
